It's been a long while (at least three years, probably more like five)
since I've played NetHack/SLASH'EM, but I just recently blew the dust off
and was playing around with a few things, just to remember how it all
works. At one point, I ran into a sleeping frost giant wearing an amulet
(which I had seen using a potion of object detection); I was using a =oC
and a nearby succubus seduced him and stole it, giving the message about
her swiping an amulet of life saving (I killed her and took it). Out of
curiosity (remember, I'm playing around trying to reacquaint myself with
the game, not trying to be a purist), I reloaded a save prior to that
point and tried to see if I could figure out a way to get the amulet off
the giant myself. I used my !oPoly and tried both a nymph and a succubus,
and used the #borrow command, and was unable to steal the amulet, or
anything else the giant was carrying. I was only able to succeed by using
my magic harp to tame the giant, who then dropped the amulet, among other
things. Surely, I must be missing something - why would the #borrow
command exist if there are no monsters you can become which can
succesfully steal items?
As a more general query, is there a spoiler page somewhere that describes
how to make the best use of various creatures you can polymorph into?
